--- a/docs/spec.md
+++ b/docs/spec.md
@@ -201,6 +201,7 @@ console.log(`Listening on ${server.url}`)
 - **Types.** `Request`: `method`, `url`, `headers`, `text()` (a `Promise<string>`), `json<T>()` (a `Promise<T, SyntaxError>`, parsed against the expected type). `Response(body?, { status?, statusText?, headers? })`, `Response.json(value, init?)`, `Response.redirect(url, status?)`, `status`, `ok`, `headers`, `text()`, `json<T>()` (promises, as on `Request`). `Headers(init?)`: `get`/`has`/`set`/`append`/`delete`/`forEach`/`toJSON`, case-insensitive; CR/LF in names and values are dropped. `URL(input, base?)` (throws `TypeError`): `href`, `protocol`, `host`, `hostname`, `port`, `pathname`, `search`, `hash`, `origin`, `searchParams`; `URL.parse`, `URL.canParse`. `URLSearchParams`: `get`/`getAll`/`has`/`set`/`append`/`delete`/`size`/`forEach`/`keys`/`values`/`toString`. `Request` also has `formData()`, `blob()`, `bytes()` and `arrayBuffer()`; a `Response` body can be a `Blob` or a `FormData`.
 - **Protocol.** HTTP/1.1 with keep-alive, pipelining, `Content-Length` and chunked request bodies, `Expect: 100-continue` and `HEAD`; `content-length` and `date` are added, and `content-type: text/plain;charset=utf-8` when a body has none. Malformed or oversized requests get `400`/`413`/`431` and are closed.
 - **Stream bodies.** `new Response(stream)` takes a `ReadableStream` made with an underlying source: `start(controller)` (`controller.enqueue(chunk)` with bytes or a string, `close()`, `error(e)`), and `cancel()`, which runs when the client leaves. The head goes out with `transfer-encoding: chunked`, and each chunk is sent as it's enqueued, so server-sent events and other incremental output work with `workers: n`. `text()` and `bytes()` on such a response read the stream whole.
+- **Request body streams.** `req.body` is a `ReadableStream | undefined` of `u8[]` chunks. A body larger than `bodyStreamThreshold` (a `Bun.serve` option, bytes) reaches the handler as soon as its head is in, and its bytes feed the stream as they arrive (Content-Length or chunked); once 512 KiB wait unread, the connection is not read until the handler takes them. `maxRequestBodySize` (bytes) answers a larger declared length with 413 and fails a chunked body past it. `text()`, `json()` and `bytes()` read the stream whole; a body nobody reads is dropped when the request is answered. A `ReadableStream` source may also have `pull(controller)`, called when a reader wants a chunk and none is queued.
